>>>markdown
# Governed analytics — interactive controls

This notebook imports `orders.malloy`. Because that model declares **givens**
(`REGION`, `STATUS`, `MIN_AMOUNT`), the Publisher UI renders a **Parameters
panel** above these cells: a region picker, a status multiselect, and a minimum
amount slider, each one the widget its declaration's control tags asked for.
Change a control and every cell re-runs with the new value. The same three
controls, from the same declarations, make up the control row on the
`governed-overview` dashboard. See [docs/givens.md](../../docs/givens.md).
>>>malloy
import "orders.malloy"
>>>markdown
## Overview dashboard

`overview` is a `# dashboard` view: KPI tiles plus a monthly trend and nested
charts. It respects whatever the Parameters panel currently has set — change any
control above and every cell re-runs.
>>>malloy
run: sales -> overview
>>>markdown
## Monthly trend
>>>malloy
run: sales -> amount_by_month
>>>markdown
## Order value by region
>>>malloy
run: sales -> by_region
>>>markdown
## Orders by status
>>>malloy
run: sales -> by_status
>>>markdown
## Order value by tenant

Note this is the *unsecured* source: `sales` scopes rows by the filter controls,
not by who is asking. `orders_secured` in `secured.malloy` is the one that gates
access by identity — see [docs/row-level-access.md](../../docs/row-level-access.md).
>>>malloy
run: sales -> by_tenant
